{"version":"1.4","group":"V101","entries":[{"id":"learn:00722886-s","headword":"capricious","group":"V101","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW000003","JBKROW002257","JBKROW026187","JBKROW030584"],"localGlosses":["변덕스러운"],"definitionEn":"determined by chance or impulse or whim rather than by necessity or reason","definitionKo":"필요나 이성보다 우연, 충동 또는 변덕에 따라 좌우되는","memoryKo":"이성보다 그때그때의 충동이 결정을 끌고 가는 모습을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"사람의 결정, 정책, 날씨처럼 변화가 자의적이고 예측하기 어려운 대상을 설명할 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단순히 '자주 바뀌는' 정도가 아니라 합리적 이유 없이 충동적으로 바뀐다는 점이 핵심입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"fickle","noteKo":"fickle은 충성·관심·감정이 쉽게 바뀜을, capricious는 결정이 변덕과 충동에 좌우됨을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The capricious policy changed without warning.","ko":"그 변덕스러운 정책은 예고 없이 바뀌었다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/capricious.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/capricious.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"cbc7bc8fb11d6d8b492bd26b5cd24ea272bcd4ca3f1ac65f6cd1505034bf946e"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0d/En-us-capricious.oga/En-us-capricious.oga.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-capricious.oga","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Paul2520"}},{"id":"learn:01288942-s","headword":"mind-boggling","group":"V101","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW000011","JBKROW003241"],"localGlosses":["놀라운"],"definitionEn":"intellectually or emotionally overwhelming","definitionKo":"지적으로나 감정적으로 압도적인","memoryKo":"마음과 머리가 멈칫할 만큼 규모나 복잡성이 압도적인 장면을 기억하세요.","usageKo":"수치, 규모, 복잡성처럼 이해하거나 받아들이기 벅찰 정도로 놀라운 것을 강조할 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"단순히 confusing한 것이 아니라 이해 범위를 넘어설 만큼 압도적이라는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"surprising","noteKo":"surprising은 예상 밖이라는 데 초점이 있고, mind-boggling은 이해하기 어려울 만큼 압도적이라는 뜻이 더 강합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The scale of the universe is mind-boggling.","ko":"우주의 규모는 정신이 아득할 만큼 압도적이다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/m/mi/mind-boggling.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/m/mi/mind-boggling.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"ecf187424df9d1182a85d39067fc4dcb1572e4816b97c98606b05b70c86c9baf"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/f/f9/En-us-mindboggling.ogg/En-us-mindboggling.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-mindboggling.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Dvortygirl"}},{"id":"learn:01074673-v","headword":"vie","group":"V101","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW000024","JBKROW003994"],"localGlosses":["얻으려고 다투다"],"definitionEn":"compete for something; engage in a contest; measure oneself against others","definitionKo":"무언가를 얻기 위해 경쟁하거나 겨루다","memoryKo":"하나의 자리나 상을 차지하려 여러 사람이 맞붙는 모습을 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"보통 vie for 형태로 상, 지위, 관심처럼 한정된 목표를 두고 치열하게 경쟁하는 문맥에 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"말다툼하다가 아니라 우위를 차지하거나 무언가를 얻기 위해 경쟁한다는 뜻입니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"compete","noteKo":"compete가 일반적인 경쟁이라면 vie는 특정 목표를 차지하려 적극적으로 다투는 느낌이 두드러집니다."}],"example":{"en":"Several candidates vied for the scholarship.","ko":"여러 지원자가 그 장학금을 두고 경쟁했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/v/vi/vie.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/v/vi/vie.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"d25b84c403eddcbd06663967a01c4c3d01a3998365249045db3064dd23ba8373"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/00/En-us-vie.oga/En-us-vie.oga.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-vie.oga","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Paul2520"}},{"id":"learn:00940267-s","headword":"callow","group":"V101","partOfSpeech":"adjective","itemIds":["JBKROW000032","JBKROW002250","JBKROW014091"],"localGlosses":["미숙한"],"definitionEn":"young and inexperienced","definitionKo":"어리고 경험이 부족한","memoryKo":"아직 경험이 익지 않은 풋내기를 떠올리세요.","usageKo":"주로 젊은 사람의 판단이나 태도가 미숙하고 세상 경험이 부족함을 나타낼 때 씁니다.","examTrapKo":"나이가 어리다는 사실만이 아니라 그로 인한 미숙함과 경험 부족을 함께 뜻합니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"naive","noteKo":"naive는 순진하거나 세상 물정을 모름을, callow는 특히 젊고 경험이 덜 익었음을 강조합니다."}],"example":{"en":"The callow reporter jumped to a conclusion.","ko":"그 미숙한 기자는 성급히 결론을 내렸다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/callow.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/c/ca/callow.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"a6ad9dea61275974e2c79dead16221424cd08f1dc3a104ffa724af35527c240c"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/de/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-callow.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_%28NaomiAmethyst%29-callow.wav.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LL-Q1860_(eng)-Naomi_Persephone_Amethyst_(NaomiAmethyst)-callow.wav","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","attribution":"Speaker: Naomi Persephone Amethyst Recorder: NaomiAmethyst"}},{"id":"learn:00884747-v","headword":"boast","group":"V101","partOfSpeech":"verb","itemIds":["JBKROW000031","JBKROW002206","JBKROW029645"],"localGlosses":["자랑하다"],"definitionEn":"show off","definitionKo":"자신을 과시하며 자랑하다","memoryKo":"자기 성취를 입 밖으로 크게 내세우는 모습을 기억하세요.","usageKo":"이 뜻에서는 사람이 자신의 능력이나 성과를 자랑스럽게 떠벌리는 행동을 가리킵니다.","examTrapKo":"사물이나 조직이 어떤 장점을 '갖추고 있다'는 boast의 다른 뜻과 구분해야 합니다.","contrasts":[{"word":"brag","noteKo":"둘 다 자랑하다이지만 brag는 흔히 지나치고 거슬리는 자랑이라는 느낌이 더 직접적입니다."}],"example":{"en":"He boasted about his perfect score.","ko":"그는 자신의 만점을 자랑했다.","kind":"editorial"},"nuance":{},"sources":[{"name":"Open English WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","license":"CC BY 4.0","edition":"2025","attribution":"Princeton WordNet; Open English WordNet Team"},{"name":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/b/bo/boast.jsonl","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0 and GFDL","edition":"checked 2026-09-04"}],"verification":{"status":"cross-agreed","reviewer":"Codex editorial cross-check","checkedAtKst":"2026.09.04","evidence":[{"source":"Open English WordNet 2025","independenceGroup":"WordNet","url":"https://en-word.net/downloads/english-wordnet-2025-json.zip","result":"agree","contentSha256":"7d749f6e2c39e6970e4997839dcf6e42fd281f3c2fae0171d2192bae8cfa4b51"},{"source":"Wiktionary via Kaikki","independenceGroup":"Wiktionary","url":"https://kaikki.org/dictionary/English/meaning/b/bo/boast.jsonl","result":"agree","contentSha256":"b760ff71615e4e4cb43a79f0db5714ae9fc1cfed46f1926aff6a2a6b0c1e9809"}]},"audio":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7f/En-us-boast.ogg/En-us-boast.ogg.mp3","region":"US","source":"Wikimedia Commons","sourcePage":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:En-us-boast.ogg","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","attribution":"Neskaya"}}]}
